label chapter_2_1:
    scene
    with Fade(0.5, 0.0, 1.0)

    nvl clear

    n "I dreamt the day before the rites."

    n "There was a TV playing another episode of Pretty Beat. Garish music emanated from its crackled speakers, and just as crackled as the speakers was Sharlene's warped singing. She sang straight gibberish. Syllables that barely strung together that then kept disintegrating into nonsensical humming. She couldn't read the karaoke lyrics on the TV at all."

    nvl clear

    shn "\"C'mon, get up and sing too! Don't you know how to have fun?\""

    n "Her shrill voice pierced my ears. Sharlene never knew how to talk at a normal volume. I always reminded her not to do it, but nothing ever stuck when it came to her."

    n "When she turned to me her face was covered in crude lipstick. She looked like a hideous creature with its mouth torn open."

    n "Yet I found my legs picking themselves up without my input. My throat expands and contracts without my will. I watched as Sofia and her small hands grabbed at some cloth, obviously hot-glued together. It tears a bit as she wraps it around herself."

    nvl clear

    shn "\"Prismmmmmm Liiiiiiive!\""

    n "Sharlene grips my hands, and brings me into a make-shift. She spins me around and twirls, trying to emulate the ballet motions on the screen."

    shn "\"Sofiaaaa! Staaaaaaardust Showerrrrrrrrr!\""

    shn "\"A... Aurora Rising...!\""

    nvl clear

    n "The world is just a spinning blur. The laughter from both Sofia and Sharlene doesn't reach my ears, and I start to feel weary of the dream. Sharlene laughs loudly. She declares us both best friends, but I can't make out the exact tones of her words. But I could feel the corners of my mouth turn up."

    n "\"Hey, even if our time now comes to an end\""

    n "\"Engrave the miracle of us being together,\""

    n "\"and moments I smiled by your side,\""

    n "\"because those simple things make up my world\""

    nvl clear

    n "When we twirl, for the final time, Sharlene laughs yet another one of her ugly laughs. I remember as she did it, she jumped so high, and I remembered that when we were even younger, she told me she always wanted to fly. When she wanted to grow up, she wanted to be a dragon, completely unbound to the earth. She looked nothing like a dragon, or even like an elegant dove, and she dived in such a strange manner, and it's there I remember,"

    n "her two front baby teeth bashed in, completely mangling her face even further. Sharlene didn't care for these things back then. She only laughed harder. She asked me if she looked terrible. The words that creak out of Sofia's throat are so strange I don't even register them as mine."

    son "\"You look... fine!\""

    nvl clear

    ssh "\"Hahahahahaha!\""

    return
